艾米跟她视如己出的谢尔顿在一起
Amy's with Sheldon who she loves like a son.

177
00:07:37,350 --> 00:07:38,830
而你跟她...
You're with her son...

178
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:41,280
视如外人的儿子在一起
who she doesn't.

179
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:45,120
你知道我们谈了五年  他才愿意给我做按摩吗
Do you realize it took me five years to get a massage from him?

180
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:49,060
那对谢尔顿来说  也算是很大的进步了
Oh, well, that still could be a big step for Sheldon.

181
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:50,620
三分钟
Three minutes.

182
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:52,930
他用了一个厨房计时器计时
And he used a kitchen timer.

183
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,940
我觉得自己就像一颗溏心蛋
I felt like a soft-boiled egg.

184
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:59,570
跟莱纳德一起相处
You know, being in a relationship with Leonard

185
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:02,130
也是挑战满满哦
also comes with its challenges.

186
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:03,140
是啊
Yes.

187
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:05,630
但你又能怎么样呢
Well, what can you do?

188
00:08:09,730 --> 00:08:12,510
或许是谢尔顿来道歉了
Maybe it's Sheldon, here to say he's sorry.

189
00:08:12,970 --> 00:08:15,260
谢尔顿说对不起
Sheldon says he's sorry.

190
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:20,260
伯纳黛特  我给你五块钱  使劲摔门
Bernadette, I'll give you five dollars to slam the door.

191
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:22,220
我收三块就行
I would have done it for three.

192
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,640
天啊  站这么久我好累啊
Boy, all this standing's making me tired.

193
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:34,320
还好我带了我的手杖折叠椅
Good thing I brought my collapsible stick chair.

194
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,040
我讨厌那椅子
Not the stick chair.

195
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:39,100
你坐在那玩意上像个傻子
You look like an idiot on that thing.

196
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:41,100
棍杖和石头或许会弄断我的骨头
Sticks and stones may break my bones,

197
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:44,310
但在棍杖上的椅子  超舒服哦
but chairs on sticks are comfy.

198
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:48,450
艾米的事摆平了吗
Is everything smoothed out with Amy?

199
00:08:48,450 --> 00:08:50,760
没有  她还是很生气
Uh, no, she's still pretty mad.

200
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:54,410
你道歉的时候  有像我那样真诚吗
Did you make the apology as sincere as I would have?

201
00:08:54,410 --> 00:08:56,820
我说"谢尔顿说对不起"
I said, "Sheldon says he's sorry."

202
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:59,750
那有点过分真诚了
Oh, well, that's laying it on a little thick.

203
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:04,510
你该亲自去跟她道歉了吧
You think it's time you apologize to her yourself?

204
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:05,880
我想也是
I suppose so.

205
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:08,090
但如果我走出队伍  我的位置就没了
But if I get out of the line, I'll lose my spot.

206
00:09:08,090 --> 00:09:10,600
我很乐意帮你保留位置等你回来
I'm happy to hold your place till you get back.

207
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,690
你会这么做吗
You would do that?

208
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:14,670
就当这是我坑你钱的方式吧
Consider it my way of getting more of your money.

209
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,810
你真是一个好人
You're a good man.

210
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:21,630
贝弗莉  你知道佩妮
So, Beverly, did you know Penny

211
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:24,270
是我们制药公司业绩第三名的销售代表吗
is the number three sales rep at our pharmaceutical company?

212
00:09:24,270 --> 00:09:26,490
我都不知道你们俩一起工作
Oh, I didn't realize you two work together.

213
00:09:26,490 --> 00:09:27,500
其实不算是
Well, we don't exactly.

214
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,630
我是研发团队的微生物学家
I'm a microbiologist for the research team.

215
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:31,200
你们最近在研发什么
Oh, what are you currently developing?

216
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:33,500
一种抗焦虑的新药
Some exciting new anti-anxiety drugs.

217
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:34,390
真是巧了
That's interesting.

218
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:37,850
我刚参加了一个关于儿童焦虑症的讲座
I just attended a lecture on pediatric anxiety.

219
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:39,680
是不是杰诺夫斯基博士的讲座
Oh, was it, uh, Dr. Jenofski?

220
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:40,960
我才看了他的TED演讲
I just saw his TED Talk!

221
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,130
正是他的
It was.

222
00:09:42,130 --> 00:09:43,550
我们还是聊回佩妮吧
Let's get back to Penny.

223
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:44,840
对了  你之前不是提起过
Hey, weren't you telling me

224
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:47,840
公司给你的那辆车有多棒吗
something great about your company car?

225
00:09:51,370 --> 00:09:53,860
车上有座椅加热器
It has seat warmers.

226
00:09:55,950 --> 00:09:57,720
艾米  艾米
Amy! Amy!

227
00:09:57,720 --> 00:10:00,280
-艾米  -进来
- Amy! - Come in.

228
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:01,370
大家好
Hello, everyone.

229
00:10:01,370 --> 00:10:02,730
贝弗利  很高兴见到你
Oh, Beverly, good to see you!

230
00:10:02,730 --> 00:10:04,520
我本想坐下来小聊一下  但是
I'd love to chat, but there's a line

231
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,460
我们排的队马上就要进场了  所以我就直说了
that could start moving any minute, so let's do this.

232
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:07,370
艾米
Amy?

233
00:10:07,370 --> 00:10:09,500
一个完整的道歉需要以下三个步骤
A proper apology requires three steps.

234
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,420
第一步  承认错误
Step one-- an admission of wrongdoing.

235
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:12,810
艾米  我错了
Amy, I was wrong.

236
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:13,800
第二步
Step two--

237
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,550
承诺再也不犯同样的错误
a promise never to repeat said action.

238
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:17,400
艾米  我再也不会犯同样的错了
Amy, that action will never be repeated,

239
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,550
我保证
and that's a promise.

240
00:10:18,570 --> 00:10:20,670
第三步  诚恳地请求对方原谅
Step three-- an earnest request for forgiveness.

241
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:22,200
艾米  求求你原谅我吧
Amy, I hope you can forgive me.

242
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,410
而且你最好快点原谅
And I hope you do it right now,

243
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:24,820
因为还有辆优步在楼下等着我呢
'cause there's an Uber waiting downstairs,

244
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:26,350
我可不想对着我的司机甘尼什
and I don't want to repeat this apology nonsense

245
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:28,770
再重复一遍无聊的道歉了
with my driver Ganesh.

246
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:32,260
原谅你了
Fine.

247
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,620
多谢了  你真是个好人
Oh, thanks! You're a peach!

248
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:34,860
贝弗利  回聊啊
Beverly, we'll catch up soon.

249
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,180
伯纳黛特  回见啊
Bernadette, it was a pleasure as always,

250
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:38,400
佩妮  你牙齿上有菠菜
Penny, you have spinach in your teeth.

251
00:10:41,170 --> 00:10:43,050
这菠菜粘在我牙齿上多久了
How long have I had spinach in my teeth?

252
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:45,330
在机场时就有了  亲
Since the airport, dear.

253
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:51,520
你看起来就像是长了个支架一样
You look like you come with a kickstand.

254
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,280
你的话伤不了我
You can't make me feel bad.

255
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,780
也许我不行  莱纳德你来
Hmm, maybe not. Leonard?

256
00:10:57,350 --> 00:10:59,340
外星人把你送回来时
So, when the aliens brought you back,

257
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:02,130
是不是忘记把探测仪拔出来了
they just left the probe in?

258
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:04,300
我回来了
I'm back.

259
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,200
-怎么样  -完美
- Hey, how'd it go? - It went well.

260
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,260
我发现如果你从来没有道过歉
Yeah, I've learned that if you never say you're sorry,

261
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:11,590
当你真的道歉时  对方可是会吓到呢
the times you do really puts them on their heels.

262
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:14,970
斯图尔特  你可以不用帮我排队了
Uh, Stuart, I relieve you of your line duties.

263
00:11:14,970 --> 00:11:16,980
还有人需要我的帮忙吗
Anyone else need anything before I go?

264
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:20,020
给你一块钱  羞辱一下拉杰
I'll give you a dollar if make fun of Raj.

265
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,050
-你太坏了  -五块钱
- That's mean. - Five.

266
00:11:22,050 --> 00:11:23,140
你好像长着尾巴的跳跳虎
You look like Tigger

267
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:25,820
如果跳跳虎和你一样像个智障的话
if Tigger looked like a jackass.

268
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,800
如果你以后需要推荐人
Uh, if you ever need a reference or anything,

269
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,040
记得找我
just let me know.

270
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:32,700
我来了
Hey, guys.

271
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:34,080
你总算赶到了
You made it.

272
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:36,510
你们看见没
Did you see that?

273
00:11:36,930 --> 00:11:37,920
他插队了
He just cut the line.

274
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:39,570
人家有朋友在排队呢  别管了
He's just joining his friends; it's fine.

275
00:11:39,570 --> 00:11:41,280
不  我才不能不管
No, it's not fine.

276
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,650
这破坏了排队的规则
It is a breach of line etiquette.

277
00:11:43,650 --> 00:11:45,010
我们差不多排在队伍的最前面了
We're near the front of the line.

278
00:11:45,010 --> 00:11:46,390
不管怎样我们都能进去
We'll get in either way.

279
00:11:46,390 --> 00:11:48,330
如果我们之前的每个人都让人插队呢
What if every person in front of us lets someone cut?

280
00:11:48,330 --> 00:11:49,200
我们也能进去
We'd still get in.

281
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,990
如果每个插队的人又让人插队呢
What if each of those people let someone cut?

282
00:11:50,990 --> 00:11:51,700
还是能进去
Still get in.

283
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:53,300
如果后来的人又让人插队呢
But then each of those people let someone cut?

284
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,930
还是能进去  但首先
We'd still get in, but first I'd hit you

285
00:11:54,930 --> 00:11:57,690
我要用他的手杖椅把你打昏
over the head with his stick chair.

286
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:01,050
-对不起  -求你别说
- Excuse me. - Oh, please don't.

287
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:03,190
我看到
Uh, uh, I couldn't help but notice

288
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:04,820
你插队了
that you cut the line.

289
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:06,610
我朋友在这排着呢
Oh, uh, I'm with my friends.

290
00:12:06,610 --> 00:12:07,360
没事
It's cool.

291
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,510
才怪
Well, no.

292
00:12:08,510 --> 00:12:09,970
这才不会没事
It's not cool.

293
00:12:10,890 --> 00:12:12,110
如果座位是预定好的
If there were reserved seating,

294
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:13,500
我们每个人都有票  那就没事
and we all had tickets, that would be fine.

295
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,650
但这队伍是谁先来谁有座
But this line is first-come, first-served.

296
00:12:15,650 --> 00:12:18,540
而不是"最后一个来  最先一个坐"
Not "Show up tardy and nevertheless be first served"

297
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:19,510
来击个掌吧
Right here.

298
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:20,890
不要
No.

299
00:12:23,230 --> 00:12:25,080
你得站到队伍最后面去
You need to go to the back of the line.

300
00:12:25,630 --> 00:12:27,970
谁批准你来当排队监督员的
Uh, who made you line monitor?

301
00:12:27,970 --> 00:12:30,470
小学四年级的旺琪老师
Mrs. Wunch in fourth grade.

302
00:12:31,590 --> 00:12:33,390
我的口号是"笔直的队伍
And my slogan was "A line that's straight

303
00:12:33,390 --> 00:12:35,250
才是好队伍"
is a line that's great""

304
00:12:37,010 --> 00:12:38,470
这家伙是认真的吗
Is this guy for real?

305
00:12:38,470 --> 00:12:41,300
老兄  我也希望他是在开玩笑
Boy, I wish I could say no.

306
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:46,150
谢尔顿愿意道歉  真是很不错
That was very nice of Sheldon to apologize.

307
00:12:46,150 --> 00:12:48,340
他已经进步很多了
Well, he's come a long way.

308
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:50,750
或者是慢慢进小碎步
Or a short way very slowly,

309
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:53,280
所以让人错觉已经是很大的进步了
so it feels like a long way.

310
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:56,990
你和他之间的关系真是太有意思了
Your relationship with him is fascinating.

311
00:12:56,990 --> 00:12:59,790
我正准备写一本有关那些事业有成的伴侣的书
I'm preparing to write a book on high-achieving couples,

312
00:12:59,790 --> 00:13:01,850
我很想采访一下你们
and I would love to interview the both of you.

313
00:13:01,850 --> 00:13:03,290
好啊
Oh, sure.

314
00:13:03,290 --> 00:13:04,950
我会告诉谢尔顿这事
I'll-I'll talk to Sheldon about it.

315
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:07,120
伯纳黛特的老公以前还当过宇航员呢
You know, Bernadette's husband is a former astronaut.

316
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,210
真的吗
Really?

317
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:09,590
你觉得他会对
Do you think he would be interested

318
00:13:09,590 --> 00:13:10,920
被采访感兴趣吗
in being interviewed as well?

319
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,880
我觉得他会感兴趣吗
Do I think he'd be interested?

320
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,820
有时候我能听到他独自躲在厕所里
Sometimes I hear him pretending to be interviewed

321
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:16,990
假装正在接受采访呢
when he's alone in the bathroom.

322
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:18,550
太好了
Wonderful!

323
00:13:18,550 --> 00:13:21,540
我会把联系方式留给你
I'll give you my contact information.

324
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:25,400
你也应该和佩妮聊聊啊
Um, you should probably talk to Penny, too.

325
00:13:26,210 --> 00:13:28,220
聊什么
About what?

326
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,890
你知道吗
Okay, you know what?

327
00:13:30,890 --> 00:13:31,860
你真是太奇葩了
This is ridiculous.

328
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:33,780
我这一天都努力跟你处好关系
I've been trying to make a connection with you all day,

329
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:36,250
明显都是白费力
and clearly I'm getting nowhere.

330
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:38,070
你是在寻求相互有种默契
Well, are you seeking a connection

331
00:13:38,070 --> 00:13:40,510
还是某种形式的承认
or just some form of validation?

332
00:13:40,510 --> 00:13:42,590
我在寻求的是一点友情
What I was seeking was some sort of friendship.

333
00:13:42,590 --> 00:13:45,330
但走到这步  我只求你不当面羞辱我就好
But at this point, I'll take you not insulting me to my face.

334
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:47,640
我的本意从不是要羞辱你
My intention was never to insult you.

335
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:48,890
你今天一整天都是这样
You've been doing it all day!

336
00:13:48,890 --> 00:13:51,060
你到底知不知道什么是羞辱
Do you even know what an insult is?!

337
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:52,980
虽然不是临床用语
Well, it's not a clinical term.

338
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,490
但举个例子  应该是你嫁给我儿子
But one example would be your marrying my son,

339
00:13:55,490 --> 00:13:57,170
没有邀请也没有告知我
and not inviting me or even telling me

340
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:59,750
要结婚这件事
the wedding was taking place.

341
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,820
好  这个例子好
Okay, good example.

342
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:10,210
乔斯·惠登的作品是如何令你觉得
What about Joss Whedon's work makes you think he'd be okay

343
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:10,210
电影《复仇者联盟》一二的导演

344
00:14:10,210 --> 00:14:12,300
破坏规则和插队是没问题的
with rule-breakers and line-cutters?!

345
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:14,650
复仇者联盟就是破坏规则者
The Avengers are rule-breakers!

346
00:14:14,650 --> 00:14:18,030
复仇二字就写在职责描述里
Being vengeful is in their job description!

347
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:20,310
他们为神盾局工作
They work for SHIELD,

348
00:14:20,310 --> 00:14:22,610
那是受美国政府管理的部门
which is a sanctioned department of the U.S. Government!

349
00:14:22,610 --> 00:14:25,400
你也为受美国政府管理的部门工作吗
Do you work for a sanctioned department of the U.S. Government?

350
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,160
其实我还真是
As a matter of fact I do.

351
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:30,940
在一个小地方叫"车辆管理局"
At a little place called the DMV.

352
00:14:32,050 --> 00:14:33,080
他说得有道理
He's got him there.

353
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,370
而且跟神盾局一样有"局"字
The D even stands for department.

354
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:37,850
大家注意
Excuse me!

355
00:14:37,850 --> 00:14:40,120
大家看这里  能不能举手表态
Excuse me, can I please see a show of hands?

356
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:43,810
认为此人插队行为有问题的请举手
Who here takes issue with this person cutting the line?

357
00:14:45,430 --> 00:14:46,880
我就说吧
Told you.

358
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:50,020
多么悲哀的世道啊
Well, what a sad state of affairs!

359
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:52,070
你们都被生活打击到
That you've all been so ground down by life,

360
00:14:52,070 --> 00:14:54,240
连有人不尊重你们都毫无知觉
you don't even notice when someone disrespects you.

361
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,720
不敢相信我们即将被揍的原因
I can't believe we're gonna get beat up,

362
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:58,390
居然不是因为你的手杖椅
and it's not because of your chair.

363
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:01,440
可知道就在现在  队伍的后面
You know, right now, at the back of this line,

364
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,350
有一个和你一样的影迷
there's a movie fan like you

365
00:15:03,350 --> 00:15:04,580
即将无法进入影厅
who's not going to get in,

366
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:07,290
就是因为这个人的不在乎
because this person simply doesn't care.

367
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:08,860
没错  在61年前的队伍里
Yeah, well, 61 years ago,

368
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:10,700
后面也站着一个人
there was another person at the back of the line

369
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:15,400
美国五六十年代的女性黑人民权运动者
因为拒绝公车司机要求黑人给白人让座的要求而被捕

370
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:15,400
她的名字就叫罗莎·帕克斯
and her name was Rosa Parks.

371
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,970
听着  你一会儿可能要装成黑人
Okay, you may have to pretend you're black

372
00:15:18,970 --> 00:15:20,940
帮我们逃过这一劫
to get us out of here.

373
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:24,430
现在让我们跟随那位勇敢女性的脚步
Now, let's follow in that brave woman's footsteps,

374
00:15:24,430 --> 00:15:26,480
为我们自己站出来吧
and stand up for ourselves!

375
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:29,350
我知道她是为了能坐下而"站起来"的
And-and I realize that she stood up by remaining seated,

376
00:15:29,350 --> 00:15:31,200
但现在不是享受这份讽刺感的时候
but now is not that time to enjoy the irony of that.

377
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,940
现在我再问一遍
Now, I ask you again.

378
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,710
如果你觉得这个人...
Who here takes issue with this person--?

379
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:37,580
我们为什么要听你讲话  你也是一个插队的
Why should we listen to you? You cut the line yourself.

380
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:39,680
我确定一定以及肯定没有
I most certainly did not.

381
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,950
我亲眼看到的
I saw you.

382
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:43,890
如果你觉得头晕
If you're feeling dizzy,

383
00:15:43,890 --> 00:15:46,910
那是因为风水轮流转
it's because the tables have turned.

384
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:51,830
你听好  我是付钱请人替我排队
Excuse me, I paid someone to wait in line for me,

385
00:15:51,830 --> 00:15:53,100
等我到达以后  他就走了
and then when I arrived, he left,

386
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:55,190
所以你这女子亲眼所见的
so what you saw, my good woman,

387
00:15:55,190 --> 00:15:57,610
叫"换"人  不叫"插"队
was "swapsies" not "cutsies"

388
00:15:57,610 --> 00:15:58,740
不行不行  等等
Oh, no, no, no, no, wait!

389
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:00,060
我再问一遍  请举手
I ask you all again. A show of hands.

390
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:02,150
谁对这个人...  别走了
Who here takes issue--? Well, stop moving!

391
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:02,960
他就要进去了
He's gonna get in!

392
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,320
-兄弟  随他吧  -不行  我做不到
- Buddy, let it go. - No, I can't.

393
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:05,260
这样不对
This isn't right.

394
00:16:05,260 --> 00:16:06,290
你已经尽力了
You did everything you could.

395
00:16:06,290 --> 00:16:08,180
不  我还能更努力
No, I could've done more.

396
00:16:09,810 --> 00:16:11,650
乖啦  你把我们对伟大人权运动先驱的
Now, now, you denigrated the memory

397
00:16:11,650 --> 00:16:13,280
美好记忆都摧毁了
of a great civil rights pioneer.

398
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:15,550
你做的已经够多了
That's all anyone could ask.

399
00:16:18,170 --> 00:16:21,980
老实说  我没有想到你居然会在乎那场婚礼
To be honest, I'm surprised you cared about the wedding at all.

400
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:24,070
我也是个人  佩妮
I'm still human, Penny.

401
00:16:24,070 --> 00:16:26,180
自己儿子的婚礼不被邀请
Not getting invited to my own son's wedding

402
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:28,140
很难不在意
is difficult to ignore.

403
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:29,430
我懂你的感受
I know how you feel.

404
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:30,660
她也没有邀请我们
She didn't invite any of us.

405
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:32,290
那是一时冲动下去结的
It was spur of the moment!

406
00:16:32,290 --> 00:16:35,550
但我们有在网上看直播
But we did get to see a live stream of it on the Internet.

407
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:38,400
我也可以看网上直播啊
I could've watched it on the Internet?

408
00:16:40,510 --> 00:16:42,260
谢你啊
Thank you.

409
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:46,320
所以如果我们邀请你去拉斯维加斯
So if we would have asked you to come to Vegas

410
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:48,890
参加我们的婚礼  你会来的吗
to see us get married, you would've come?

411
00:16:48,890 --> 00:16:51,530
不会  我会说你们犯了滔天大错
No, I would've said you're making a huge mistake.

412
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:54,730
但邀请一下也算礼数做到了啊
But an invitation would've been nice.

413
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:58,170
你真觉得我们是错误吗
You really think we made a mistake?

414
00:16:58,170 --> 00:16:59,480
当时我是那么认为的
At the time I did.

415
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:02,220
但我从来没见过莱纳德那么开心
But I-I've never seen Leonard so happy,

416
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:05,600
所以  也许是我错了
so... perhaps I was wrong.

417
00:17:08,370 --> 00:17:08,940
好吧
Okay.

418
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,180
那这样吧
Well, um, how about this?

419
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:12,660
趁着你还在城里
Maybe while you're still in town,

420
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:16,090
我跟莱纳德再办一次小仪式
Leonard and I could have another small ceremony.

421
00:17:16,090 --> 00:17:18,760
如果你想参加的话
You know, if you're interested.

422
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:21,430
我完全可以接受
I would find that perfectly acceptable.

423
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:24,370
她说完全可以接受
She would find it perfectly acceptable!

424
00:17:24,370 --> 00:17:26,890
你们看到了吧  我们婆媳情深
You guys saw it! We bonded!

425
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,330
华仔  你没事吧
Howie? You doing okay?

426
00:17:37,330 --> 00:17:38,970
你已经在里面待很久了
You've been in there a while.

427
00:17:38,970 --> 00:17:41,240
没事  马上出去
I'm fine. Be right out.

428
00:17:43,470 --> 00:17:45,400
我算不算美国英雄
Am I an American hero?

429
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:50,430
真是个好问题  吉姆
Well, that's a good question, Jim.

430
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:54,460
你不觉得一位宇航员一旦离开了地球
Don't you think once an astronaut leaves the planet,

431
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:58,640
就成为世界英雄了吗
he's a hero to all the nations of the Earth?

432
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:02,690
好的
Okey dokey.

433
00:18:02,690 --> 00:18:05,730
我应该还有空回答最后一道问题
I think I have time for one more question.

